2. ARCHITECTURE & STACK
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Backend: Django 5 + Django REST Framework + Django Channels (ASGI).
  Served by gunicorn with a uvicorn worker (config.asgi:application), so one
  container serves HTTP + WebSockets.
- Frontend: Next.js 16 (Turbopack). Three build modes (frontend/next.config.mjs):
    * default             -> static export (output: 'export') to out/  (Amplify)
    * DOCKER_STANDALONE=1 -> standalone server (.next/standalone)       (Docker)
    * VERCEL=1            -> standard Next build
- Database: PostgreSQL + pgvector (embedding vectors + HNSW index); SQLite
  fallback for local/dev. Vector column width comes from EMBED_DIM at migration
  time and MUST match the embedding model.
- Cache / rate limiting: Django cache (LocMem by default, Redis via CACHE_URL).
- Channel layer (team chat WebSockets): InMemoryChannelLayer by default,
  channels-redis when CACHE_URL is set. In-memory works ONLY with 1 instance.
- Background work: Celery when CELERY_BROKER_URL is set; otherwise indexing
  falls back to a daemon thread in the web process (SYNC_INDEXING=true forces
  inline). Celery beat schedule: requeue_stuck_documents every 15 min,
  prune_asklogs daily 03:15. Prod compose runs api + worker + beat + web + db
  + redis (worker --concurrency=2).
- Infra-as-code: infra/ Terraform (ECS Fargate, RDS Postgres, Redis, ALB+ACM,
  SES, ECR, S3, IAM OIDC for CI, observability module). NEVER APPLIED — design
  only. validated + Checkov-passing.
- CI (.github/workflows): backend tests + coverage, frontend tests/build,
  Docker build + Trivy scan, bandit, pip-audit, gitleaks, terraform validate +
  tflint + checkov. deploy.yml builds/pushes ECR images with GitHub OIDC.

