8. DEPLOYMENT PLAN (simplest paid AWS path — chosen 2026-11-18)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Full step-by-step: docs/DEPLOY_AWS_SIMPLE.md. Build spec: amplify.yml (root).

Shape:  Amplify Hosting (frontend) + AWS App Runner (backend, container from
        ECR) + Amazon RDS PostgreSQL 16 (db.t4g.micro, pgvector) + Amazon S3
        (documents; App Runner disk is ephemeral) + Google Gemini (AI).

Cost:   ~$20–30/month total (~$40–60 for two months) before AI tokens.
        Amplify ~$1–3, App Runner ~$5–10, RDS ~$13–15, S3 ~$1.

Key decisions / answers:
- PRIVATE GitHub repo is fine for both Amplify and App Runner.
- Elastic Beanstalk IS possible but is more wiring (no push-to-deploy for a
  private repo without CodePipeline; RDS/S3 still separate) — App Runner chosen.
- App Runner SOURCE deploys do NOT work for this backend (managed runtime lacks
  tesseract/poppler/libpq) — build the image and deploy from ECR.
- Backend container: 0.25 vCPU / 0.5 GB, port 8000, health check HTTP
  /api/health (exempt from the HTTPS redirect). ASGI serves HTTP+WS.
- VPC connector on DEFAULT (public) subnets: reaches private RDS AND the
  internet for Gemini without a ~$32/mo NAT gateway.
- Instance role for S3 (no static AWS keys anywhere).
- Keep App Runner at 1 instance until Redis is added (WebSockets + rate limits
  are per-instance).

Critical backend env vars (App Runner):
  ENVIRONMENT=production, DEBUG=false, SECRET_KEY=<random>,
  LLM_KEY_ENCRYPTION_KEY=<random, back it up>,
  ALLOWED_HOSTS=<apprunner host>, CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS / CSRF_TRUSTED_ORIGINS /
  PUBLIC_BASE_URL = https://<amplify-domain>,
  DATABASE_URL=postgresql://...?sslmode=require,
  AWS_STORAGE_BUCKET_NAME=<bucket>, AWS_S3_REGION_NAME=<region>,
  LLM_PROVIDER=gemini, GEMINI_API_KEY=<key>,
  EMBED_PROVIDER=gemini, EMBED_DIM=3072,
