9. SECURITY, SAFEGUARDS & KNOWN LANDMINES
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Safeguards integrated (all real code):
- Tenant isolation: company-scoped querysets everywhere + an 18-case isolation
  matrix test (IDOR probes, cross-tenant chunk leaks, path traversal).
- Auth: JWT 15-min access / 7-day rotating+blacklisted refresh; TOTP MFA;
  email verification gate; password reset.
- Hardening (settings.py): HSTS 1y+subdomains+preload, SSL redirect (health
  exempt), X-Frame-Options DENY, nosniff, SameSite=Lax HttpOnly cookies,
  production boot guard refusing ALLOWED_HOSTS=*.
- OriginCheckMiddleware (CSRF defence-in-depth for the cookie-JWT auth path).
- Ratelimit: atomic cache-backed counters; trusting only TRUSTED_PROXY_COUNT
  X-Forwarded-For entries.
- netguard.py: SSRF defence for tenant-supplied base_url (public IPs only,
  metadata range blocked).
- crypto.py: Fernet encryption at rest for BYO provider keys (rotation caveats
  documented; docs/SECURITY.md has a zero-downtime rotation runbook).
- moderation.py: policy-violation scanner (docs say honestly: regex is NOT a
  prompt-injection barrier) + structural defences (permission filtering, no
  tools, citation-grounded answers).
- qr_tokens.py: signed, short-lived, company-bound QR attendance tokens.
- Supply chain: bandit, pip-audit, Trivy, gitleaks in CI; zero GPL/AGPL deps;
  GitHub OIDC in CI (no long-lived AWS keys); secrets via SSM in the ECS path.

